  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 147 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nHeat will continue to be our main concern over the next week. An \nExtreme Heat Warning remains in effect areawide through Friday. The \nExtreme Heat Warning will be maintained for the southern tier or two \nof counties (roughly Rushville to Robinson south) where peak indices \nwill linger near or above 105F, however elsewhere isn't exactly\ncooling down significantly. Heat indices north of the warning \nremain around 100 degrees. \n\nA backdoor cold front will push into the area late Saturday \nafternoon, which could bring \"relief\" Sunday and Monday, where heat \nindices will be in the low to mid 90s, rather than over 100, and \nhighs in the upper 80s to low 90s. These, so-called, cooler \ntemperatures will warm back up to mid to upper 90s by mid next week \nbefore backing off again by the end of the week.\n\nWe will continue to be in record territory for temperatures as this \nearly September heat wave persists. Check out the climate section \nbelow for more details. \n\nThe SPC has removed the marginal risk for severe weather for central \nIL for today. A rogue shower or thunderstorm is not out of the \nquestion for the day today. However, the chances are quite low (< \n20%) areawide for any activity. Despite decent CAPE values, forecast \nsoundings show a very dry profile and low bulk shear values. Beyond \ntoday, the next potential for any rain activity comes late next week \nas the upper ridging pattern appears to break down.",
